    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where requests complete with plausible-looking outputs despite underlying faults.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical system.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must match. Verify the hash of the *loaded* artifact, not just the file on disk (catches corrupted downloads, partial loads, or divergent sharding).\n- [ ] **Sharding plan identity.** If weights are sharded (TP/PP/EP), record the sharding manifest: layer-to-rank mapping, expert placement, and the code version that generated it. Confirm all nodes agree on the plan.\n- [ ] **Code and dependency versions.** Capture commit hashes, container image digests, and versions of the inference engine, CUDA/ROCm, NCCL/Gloo, and driver stack on every node. Diff across nodes; any difference is a finding.\n- [ ] **Deterministic-relevant settings.** Record sampling parameters, seed handling, KV-cache configuration, quantization settings, and any kernel-selection heuristics (e.g., cuBLAS workspace, flash-attention backend). Note that these may legitimately differ per node in data-parallel setups \u2014 but must be identical across ranks within a single replicated group.\n- [ ] **Launch configuration.** Verify the distributed init (rank count, world size, master address/port, backend) matches the intended topology. Confirm no stale processes from prior runs are attached (check `nvidia-smi` / process",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
